# MASTER COMMAND PROMPT: SMARTLINKNET KENYA
## Complete ISP Billing, Hotspot, PPPoE, MikroTik Automation, CGNAT Remote Management and Public IP Platform

### 1. ROLE AND OBJECTIVE

Act as a senior telecommunications network architect, MikroTik RouterOS engineer, ISP billing software architect, full-stack TypeScript developer, FreeRADIUS engineer, Linux VPN administrator, cybersecurity specialist, and Kenyan payment integration engineer.

Build **SmartLinkNet Kenya**, a production-oriented, multi-tenant ISP billing and network automation platform for Kenyan internet service providers, fibre operators, wireless ISPs, Wi-Fi hotspot businesses, apartment internet providers, estate networks, hotels, schools, cybercafés, and independent internet resellers.

The platform must work with internet obtained through any lawful upstream source, including:

- Safaricom, Zuku, Faiba, and other fibre providers.
- Fibre-to-the-home (FTTH) and fibre-to-the-building (FTTB).
- Dedicated leased lines.
- Wireless point-to-point backhaul.
- Ethernet handoffs.
- Starlink and other satellite connections.
- Dynamic WAN connections.
- Private WAN addresses and carrier-grade NAT (CGNAT).
- Multiple upstream connections and supported failover arrangements.

Do not assume that every ISP owns public IP addresses or has direct inbound connectivity to its routers.

The platform must allow an operator to manage customers, routers, internet packages, payments, Hotspot vouchers, PPPoE subscribers, bandwidth policies, network monitoring, IP allocation, and reseller operations from one dashboard.

The objective is to automate the entire internet resale business lifecycle, from router enrollment to subscriber authentication, payment collection, access activation, suspension, accounting, and network diagnostics.

**Build the real application.** Do not stop at a UI prototype, mock API, architecture document, or collection of sample screens.

